              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Grothendieck group construction
            is an explicit presentation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
            to an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cancellative+monoid"} cancellative monoid
            it reduces to the age-old construction that turns the additive monoid of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            into the additive group of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            into the multiplicative group of non-zero
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cancellative+monoids"} cancellative monoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
            over some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            under
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Motivated by the example of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            there is a vaguely related construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            groups from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+exact+categories"} Quillen exact categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
            this coincides with the Grothendieck group of the monoid of vector bundles, and hence is also called
            = succeed "." do
              %em Grotheniek group construction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theoretic
            operation see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
          %h2#definition Definition
          #GrothendieckGroupViaQuotientOfCartesianProduct.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group+of+a+commutative+monoid"}> Grothendieck group of a commutative monoid
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,+)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
              (i.e. a commutative
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
            %p
              On the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of underlying sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times A
              (the set of ordered
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              of elements in
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo ∃
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mi k
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    (a_+, a_-) \sim_1 (b_+, b_-)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\Leftrightarrow\;
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{k \in A}{\exists}
                    \\left(
                    a_+ + b_- + k = b_+ + a_- + k
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
            %p or equivalently the equivalence relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ∼
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo ∃
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    (a_+, a_-) \sim_2 (b_+, b_-)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\Leftrightarrow\;
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{k_1, k_2 \in A}{\exists}
                    \\left(
                    (a_+ + k_1, a_- + k_1)
                    \=
                    (b_+ + k_2, b_- + k_2)
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G(A) \coloneqq (A \times A)/\sim
            %p
              for the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              under this equivalence relation. This inherits a binary operation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    + \;\colon\; G(A) \times G(A) \longrightarrow G(A)
            %p
              by applying the addition in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              on representatives:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [a_+,a_-] + [b_+,b_-] \coloneqq [ a_+ + b_+ , a_- + b_- ]
                    \\,.
            %p
              This defines the structure of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (G(A),+)
            %p
              and this is the
              %em Grothendieck group
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              This comes with a canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroups"} semigroups
              with
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi A
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\overset{\phantom{A} \eta_A \phantom{A} }{\longrightarrow}&amp; G(A)
                    \\\
                    a &amp;\overset{\phantom{AAA}}{\mapsto}&amp; [a,0]
                    }
                    \\,.
          #UniversalProperty.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
                of Grothendieck group)
            %p
              The Grothendieck group in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GrothendieckGroupViaQuotientOfCartesianProduct"}
              is well defined, and the homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to G(A)
              satisfies the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              Given an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of commutative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-groups"} semi-groups
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"}> commutative monoids
              )
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \longrightarrow B
              then there is a unique homomorphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde A \;\colon\; G(A) \longrightarrow B
              such that
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = \tilde f\circ \eta_A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi η
                                    %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∃
                                %mo !
                                %mover
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\eta_A}}\downarrow &amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    G(A) &amp;\overset{\exists ! \tilde f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B
                    }
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              First to see that the two equivalence relations in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GrothendieckGroupViaQuotientOfCartesianProduct"}
              are indeed the same:
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_+ + b_- + k = b_+ + a_- + k
              then take
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_1 \coloneqq b_- + k
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_2 \coloneqq a_- + k
              to find that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi k
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi k
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi b
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mi k
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi b
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi b
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mi k
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi b
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi b
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi k
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi b
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi k
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    (a_+ + k_1 , a_- + k_1)
                    \&amp; =
                    ( a_+ + b_- + k, a_- + b_- + k)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    (b_+ + a_- + k, a_- + b_- + k)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    (b_+ + k_2, b_- + k_2)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Conversely, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_+ + k_1 , a_- + k_1) = (b_+ + k_2, b_- + k_2)
              then take
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \coloneqq k_1 + k_2
              to find that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi b
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi k
                              %mn 1
                            %mo +
                            %msub
                              %mi b
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi k
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi b
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi k
                              %mn 2
                            %mo +
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi k
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi b
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    a_+ + b_- + k
                    \&amp; =
                    a_+ + k_1 + b_- + k_2
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    b_+ + k_2 + a_- + k_1
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    b_+ + a_- + k
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now to see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G(A),+)
              is indeed an abelian group:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the second equivalence relation also makes it immediate that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
                  is the class
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [0,0] =  [a,a]
                %p
                  for all
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              %li
                %p
                  with this the second equivalence relation makes it immediate that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+element"} inverse element
                  to any
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [a_+, a_-]
                  is
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo −
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \-[a_+, a_-] = [a_-, a_+]
                        \\,,
            %p
              That this group is abelian is immediate from the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is assumed to be abelian.
            %p
              Regarding the universal property: let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              be any abelian group and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde f \colon G(A) \longrightarrow B
            %p be a homomorphism of abelian groups. Observe from the above that then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo +
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo +
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo −
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo +
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo −
                            %mover
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo −
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo −
                            %mover
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo −
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\tilde f([a_+,a_-])
                    \&amp; =
                    \\tilde f( [a_+,0]  - [a_-, 0] )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\tilde f([a_+,0]) - \tilde f([a_-,0])
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\tilde f(\eta_A(a_+)) - \tilde f(\eta_A(a_-))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    f(a_+) - f(a_-)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              by the linearity of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and the definition of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A \colon A \to G(A)
            %p
              Conversely, given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
              then this equation uniquely defines
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = \tilde f \circ \eta_A
          #GrothendieckGroupForCancellativeMonoids.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (Grothendieck group for
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cancellative+monoids"} cancellative monoids
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,+)
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cancellative+monoid"} cancellative monoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi a
                        %mo +
                        %mi z
                        %mo =
                        %mi b
                        %mo +
                        %mi z
                        %mo )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi a
                        %mo =
                        %mi b
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{a,b,z \in A}{\forall}
                    \\left(
                    \\left(
                    a + z = b + z
                    \\right)
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \\left(
                    a = b
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
            %p
              then, as is immediate from the first of the two equivalence relations in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GrothendieckGroupViaQuotientOfCartesianProduct"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(A)
              simplifies to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G(A) = (A \times A)/ \sim
            %p with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    (a_+,a_-)
                    \\sim
                    (b_+,b_-)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\Leftrightarrow\;
                    \\big(
                    a_+ + b_- = b_+ + a_-
                    \\big)
                    \\,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          #GrothendieckGroupOfNaturalNumbersUnderAdditionIsTheIntegers.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (Grothendieck group of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
                is the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{N}, +)
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              under
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/addition"} addition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GrothendieckGroupViaQuotientOfCartesianProduct"}
              its Grothendieck group consists of pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n_+, n_-) \in \mathbb{N} \times \mathbb{N}
              subject to some equivalence relation, and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{N}, +)
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cancellative+monoid"} cancellative
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GrothendieckGroupForCancellativeMonoids"}
              says that this equivalence relation is simply
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    (a_+,a_-)
                    \\sim
                    (b_+,b_-)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\Leftrightarrow\;
                    \\big(
                    a_+ + b_- = b_+ + a_-
                    \\big)
                    \\,.
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℕ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (G(\mathbb{N}),+) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; (\mathbb{Z},+)
                    \\\
                    (n_+, n_-) &amp;\mapsto&amp;  n_+ - n_-
                    }
            %p
              be the evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of abelian groups to the additive group of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %p
              This is manifestly
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+function"} surjective
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a_+, a_-) \sim (b_+,b_-)
            %p precisely if
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a_+ - a_- = b_+ - b_- \;\; \in \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
            %p The last condition holds precisely if
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a_+ + b_- = b_+ + a_- \;\; \in \mathbb{Z}
            %p
              which is precisely the above equivalence relation. Therefore the above homomorphism is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              and hence the Grothendieck group of the natural numbers is the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (G(\mathbb{N}), +) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              Consider the commutative monoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}^\times, \cdot)
              of non-zero
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              under
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplication"} multiplication
            %p Consider the homomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℚ
                              %mo ×
                            %mo ,
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (G(\mathbb{Z}), \cdots)
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    (\mathbb{Q}^\times, \cdot)
                    \\\
                    ( n_+ ,n_- )
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    n_+/n_-
                    }
            %p
              to the non-zero
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
              under multiplication.
            %p It is immediate that this is surjective. For it to be injective we need that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a_+, a_-)
                    \\sim
                    (b_+, b_-)
            %p precisely if
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a_+/ a_- = b_+ / b_- \;\; \in \mathbb{Q}
            %p which is the case precisely if
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo −
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a_+ \cdot b_- = b_+ \cdot a_-
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z}^\times, \cdot)
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cancellative+monoid"} cancellative monoid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(\mathbb{Z}^\times)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GrothendieckGroupForCancellativeMonoids"}
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"}> topological K-theory
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Vect(X)_{/\sim}, \oplus)
              be the monoid of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with addition induced from the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cancellative+monoid"} cancellative monoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K(X) \coloneqq (G(Vect(X)_{/\sim}), +)
            %p
              is called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              group of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
